comments.message:
The creation guard fires for **any non-IANA field**, including `PLDM_FRU_FIELD_TYPE_VENDOR`, `PLDM_FRU_FIELD_TYPE_CHASSIS`, etc... — all of which hit `break` in the switch and set **no** D-Bus properties.

In a scenario where a terminus has only these unhandled fields, we would still get empty decorator interfaces registered on D-Bus. 

I would suggest move the creation guard inside only the cases that actually set a property in the form of a helper function that initializes the decorator interface only if it doesn't already exist.

Something like

```
		case PLDM_FRU_FIELD_TYPE_MODEL:
			initFruDecoratorIfNotExist();
			fruDecoratorsIntf->model(fruField);
			break;
		case PLDM_FRU_FIELD_TYPE_PN:
			initFruDecoratorIfNotExist();
			fruDecoratorsIntf->partNumber(fruField);
			break;
		case PLDM_FRU_FIELD_TYPE_SN:
			initFruDecoratorIfNotExist();
			fruDecoratorsIntf->serialNumber(fruField);
			break;
```
